 "intro": [
  "Abraham, \"father of a multitude of nations\" (17:5), has sons by three women. Ishmael's twelve sons parallel the twelve sons of Jacob; Keturah's sons are the peoples of the Arabian incense and caravan routes (Midian, Sheba, Dedan). The chosen line runs through Isaac to the twins Esau and Jacob."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Rashi on Genesis 25; Genesis Rabbah 61; Josephus, Antiquities 1.238–241. Scholarly identifications after the standard commentaries and reference works.",
